nthia Lummis (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Cynthia Lummis's retirement hands Republicans an open seat in one of the nation's most Republican states, and Trump-backed Harriet Hageman cleared the GOP primary in a landslide. James Byrd, a Democratic state legislator, faces a steep financial deficit: Hageman has raised $2.4 million with roughly $1 million in outside support, while Byrd has raised about $23,000 and reports just $356 on hand. Every major rating outlet rates the race Safe or Solid for Republicans, and prediction markets put a Byrd win at one to two percent.\n\nHageman is favored by roughly 20 points. Her primary dominance, name recognition, and overwhelming money advantage more than offset a national environment tilted toward Democrats in a state with a 23-point Republican lean. No general-election polling exists for this race, but recent statewide margins for Wyoming Republicans suggest the edge could be larger still.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0087, "margin": -17.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0045, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0066, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0194, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0012, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0022, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0049, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0042, "margin": -19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0062, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0024, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0026, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0068, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0098, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0029, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0026, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0024, "margin": -20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0009, "margin": -25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0039, "ma